<EXPERIMENT_PACKAGE><EXPERIMENT alias="GSM2638038" accession="SRX2848435"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRX2848435</PRIMARY_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>GSM2638038: Normal_PR_2.TR03; Homo sapiens; RNA-Seq</TITLE><STUDY_REF accession="SRP107937" refname="GSE99248"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRP107937</PRIMARY_ID></IDENTIFIERS></STUDY_REF><DESIGN><DESIGN_DESCRIPTION/><SAMPLE_DESCRIPTOR accession="SRS2221041"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS2221041</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM2638038</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS></SAMPLE_DESCRIPTOR><LIBRARY_DESCRIPTOR><LIBRARY_STRATEGY>RNA-Seq</LIBRARY_STRATEGY><LIBRARY_SOURCE>TRANSCRIPTOMIC</LIBRARY_SOURCE><LIBRARY_SELECTION>cDNA</LIBRARY_SELECTION><LIBRARY_LAYOUT><PAIRED/></LIBRARY_LAYOUT><LIBRARY_CONSTRUCTION_PROTOCOL>collection protocol: For each donor eye, the retina (PR) and RPE-Choroid-Sclera (PRCS) samples were dissected from the peripheral region of the posterior eye globes using a 10mm-biopsy punch followed by a 8mm-punch in the middle of the 10mm-punch to minimize the sample contamination. A total of 32 RNA samples were prepared using the AllPrep DNA/RNA Mini kit (Qiagen). Library preparation and sequencing was done using the TruSeq Stranded total RNA with RiboZero Gold kit (Illumina, CA) protocol with a total RNA (800ng) as the starting material.</LIBRARY_CONSTRUCTION_PROTOCOL></LIBRARY_DESCRIPTOR></DESIGN><PLATFORM><ILLUMINA><INSTRUMENT_MODEL>Illumina HiSeq 2000</INSTRUMENT_MODEL></ILLUMINA></PLATFORM><EXPERIMENT_LINKS><EXPERIMENT_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>gds</DB><ID>302638038</ID><LABEL>GSM2638038</LABEL></XREF_LINK></EXPERIMENT_LINK></EXPERIMENT_LINKS><EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTES><EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>GEO Accession</TAG><VALUE>GSM2638038</VALUE></EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTE></EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTES></EXPERIMENT><SUBMISSION alias="GEO: GSE99248" broker_name="GEO" center_name="GEO" submission_comment="submission brokered by GEO" lab_name="" accession="SRA565550"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRA565550</PRIMARY_ID><SUBMITTER_ID namespace="GEO">GEO: GSE99248</SUBMITTER_ID></IDENTIFIERS></SUBMISSION><Organization type="center"><Name abbr="GEO">NCBI</Name><Contact email="geo-group@ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"><Name><First>Geo</First><Last>Curators</Last></Name></Contact></Organization><STUDY center_name="GEO" alias="GSE99248" accession="SRP107937"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRP107937</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioProject" label="primary">PRJNA387704</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSE99248</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_TITLE>Comparsion of the transcriptome profiles in normal and age-related macular degneration in retina and RPE-Choroid-Scleral (RCS) tissues</STUDY_TITLE><STUDY_TYPE existing_study_type="Transcriptome Analysis"/><STUDY_ABSTRACT>Analysis of retinal and RCS tissues revealed a significant differential expression of noncoding RNA and anti-sense transcripts in AMD when compared to the normal tissues. Overall design: The retinal and RPE-Choroid-Scleral tissue punches from Eight normal and Eight age-related macular degeneration donor eye samples were obtained and processed within 8hrs from the time of death. The total RNA was isolated using Qiagen All prep kit and RNA libraries were made using Illumina Stranded-Sequencing Ribozero kit. The prepared RNA libaries were multiplexed and PE100bp sequencing was performed on Illumina HiSeq2000. The complete RNA transcriptome is analyzed by a standardized in-house bioinformatic pipeline and the results are interpreted.</STUDY_ABSTRACT><CENTER_PROJECT_NAME>GSE99248</CENTER_PROJECT_NAME></DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_LINKS><STUDY_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>pubmed</DB><ID>29445097</ID></XREF_LINK></STUDY_LINK></STUDY_LINKS></STUDY><SAMPLE alias="GSM2638038" accession="SRS2221041"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS2221041</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN07161009</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM2638038</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>Normal_PR_2.TR03</TITLE><SAMPLE_NAME><TAXON_ID>9606</TAXON_ID><SCIENTIFIC_NAME>Homo sapiens</SCIENTI